# robots.txt for <%= SiteMetadata.origin %>
#
# AI and LLM crawlers are allowed. That is a decision, not a default that nobody
# got round to overriding, and it is written here because this file is the only
# place a reader will think to look for it.
#
# This site exists to be found. A large share of its readers arrive through a
# search result or through an assistant answering someone's question about the
# person it describes, and an assistant that cannot read this page answers from
# something worse — a stale profile, a scraped aggregator, a guess. So GPTBot,
# ClaudeBot, Google-Extended, PerplexityBot, CCBot, Applebot-Extended and
# whatever succeeds them are covered by the wildcard below deliberately. The
# absence of a Disallow for any of them is the policy.
#
# There is nothing here to protect. Every byte a crawler can reach was curated
# for publication and passes the scan in features/curated-content/SPEC.md.
#
# The one exclusion is the container health check, which renders no content and
# exists for the proxy.

User-agent: *
Allow: /
Disallow: <%= rails_health_check_path %>

Sitemap: <%= SiteMetadata.sitemap_url %>
